  "rules": {
    "C": "C(arm) = median over cells of dM_main - dM_round",
    "S": "S(arm) = #cells where the donor-new-source patch is JOINT and the donor-ROUND-source patch of the same arm is not (target host new)",
    "SPEC": "SPEC iff dM_main > dM_round in >= 75% of cells AND in a majority of cells for >= 10 of 14 donor groups",
    "SUF": "SUF(arm) iff S(arm) >= 1/2 S(full) and SPEC(arm)",
    "always_reported": "S, SPEC, J_main, J_round, median dM and C per arm; the (t, s) grid of S and C; per host; leave-one-donor-group-out of every verdict; energy shares, alpha and capped share of the contrast parts; change norm of every arm relative to the full patch; the M8 / M7 replay counts",
    "consistency_gate": "full = the M3 all-heads patch: its 208 rows equal M3's bitwise and S(full) = 51; meanD_host = the M6 pooled-donor arm: its 208 rows equal M6's bitwise and S = 39 (GPU, checked in the run); cs0 / cs05 / cs1 / cs2 = the M8 arms (same patch fields): their 832 rows equal M8's bitwise and S = 0 / 38 / 39 / 36; otherwise every verdict is INCONSISTENT_WITH_M3_M6_M8 and no claim. g0_2 against the M7 rcD rows (bitwise and S) is reported, not gated",
    "contrast_heads_verdict": "on cs1 with the contrast restricted to head slices: CONTRAST_IN_WRITER_HEADS iff SUF(chW) and not SUF(chR); CONTRAST_OUTSIDE_WRITER_HEADS iff SUF(chR) and not SUF(chW); CONTRAST_EITHER_HEAD_SET iff both; CONTRAST_NEEDS_ALL_HEADS iff neither. Suffix +H10 iff SUF(ch10)",
    "contrast_subspace_verdict": "CONTRAST_IN_COMMON_SUBSPACE iff SUF(cpar16_sm) and not SUF(cperp16_sm); CONTRAST_OUTSIDE_COMMON_SUBSPACE iff SUF(cperp16_sm) and not SUF(cpar16_sm); CONTRAST_BOTH_PARTS iff both; CONTRAST_NOT_SPLITTABLE iff neither; suffix _UNRESOLVED on the first three if SPLIT_NULL fails",
    "gain_shape_verdict": "for s in 1, 2: L(s) = (C(g05_s) - C(g0_s)) / (C(cs_s) - C(g0_s)), defined iff C(cs_s) - C(g0_s) > 0. GAIN_BILINEAR iff both L in [0.3, 0.7]; GAIN_EARLY_SATURATING iff both > 0.7; GAIN_LATE_THRESHOLD iff both < 0.3; GAIN_MIXED otherwise; GAIN_UNDEFINED if either is undefined. The quarter-point ratios Q(s) (g025 in place of g05) are reported",
    "gain_tmin_verdict": "t* = the smallest t in 0, 1/4, 1/2, 1 with SUF(g{t}_1) (cs1 at t = 1); GAIN_TMIN:t*, or GAIN_TMIN_NONE. The SUF set over the whole (t, s) grid is reported",
    "interpretation_fixed_in_advance": "GAIN_BILINEAR: the contrast's effect on the margin grows in proportion to the common shift (a product). GAIN_EARLY_SATURATING: half the common shift already gives most of it. GAIN_LATE_THRESHOLD: little effect until the full common shift. GAIN_TMIN:t: the smallest common shift at which the contrast at s = 1 repairs. CONTRAST_IN_WRITER_HEADS: the contrast acts through the o_proj-input slice of the M3 writer heads 8-14, not the others; +H10: head 10's slice alone suffices. CONTRAST_EITHER_HEAD_SET / CONTRAST_NEEDS_ALL_HEADS: the contrast is not localized to one head set. CONTRAST_IN_COMMON_SUBSPACE: at matched size, the part of c inside the 16-dim common subspace repairs and the part outside does not (the contrast is aligned with the common part); CONTRAST_OUTSIDE_COMMON_SUBSPACE: the reverse. All M9 arms are pooled-donor arms (effectively 8 host replicates); per-host S is the honest unit. The head arms are not size-matched (slice energies reported). Since M8 found that a quarter of c per source already repairs, a part with a large share of c's energy may pass on size alone; the split arms are size-matched for this reason",
    "readouts": "M = conflict margin; A = logit(reject_conflict) - max(accept, wait); JOINT = M > 0 and A > 0; dM = M(patch) - M(in-run capture of host new)",
    "size_gate": "per row and span position where alpha < cap, the rescaled contrast part has norm ||c|| within 1e-3 relative (fail-closed in the runner); alpha = min(||c|| / ||part||, 10) (random frame: no cap); energy share sum ||part||^2 / sum ||c||^2, alpha and the capped share are recorded, as are the energy shares of the head slices",
    "split_null": "SPLIT_NULL holds iff S(crand16_sm) <= 5 and not SPEC(crand16_sm)",
    "units": "the 104 cross-group cells of M1-M6; cells share donors and hosts, and the pooled-mean arms vary with the donor only through the pool exclusion (effectively 8 hosts), so counts are descriptive decision rules, not independent tests; per-host S is always reported"
  },
